From 02f74927ab675aff68675bc6ce6078bad36e625e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 03:11:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 097/112] Filters: the LP ladders' ramps at about v17's cost
 per sample

The heavy test song ramps every synth's 24 dB ladder every block (envelopes, LFOs); the ramp loop cost 83
instructions per sample (v17's plain loop about 60), mostly spills. Now 55 (precise) per sample:

- The 24 dB and drive ladders take their feedback in a ramp from the moving moveability and
  divideBy1PlusTannedFrequency (Horner: d / 4 * (2 s4 + G (s3 + G (s2 + G s1))), feedbackFromMoveability()): three
  coefficients fewer to move, and every sample's feedback that of a real ladder for its G and d. Where the input is a
  tanh's (bounded to 2^27) and the stages precise (G < 1/4), without the halvings.
- The coefficients step once per pair of samples (both take the pair's second set; the last sample still lands on
  the target): a staircase at Nyquist of two samples' change, sets on the same line (lpf_ramp_math models it,
  0.39 dB, stable).
- A one-piece ramp (the usual) skips the knots; its steps only for what the loop reads (stepsFor()); stride a
  template parameter; the 12 / 24 dB break frequency found once instead of two instantTan() per block.
- Spec 7: a change under 0.5 cent (resonance / morph under 2^-13 of their range) takes no ramp (rampAudible(), LP, HP
  ladder, SVF): a step nobody hears, the ramp's cost only where needed.

Full song (song_emu --init-sounds --seed 1): demand 102.0 % -> 90.8 % (v17 89.3 % in the same run), filters
484k -> 352k per 128 samples (v17 338k); device: FORCE culls 7 (v17 13), SOFT 106 (98), mean voices 31.2 (31.7).
Hashes demand 4b2736026f83707e, digital 239b71379d508cfc (the ladders' ramps and precise stages round differently).

